{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>YHWH my Elohim.</b> The words of the prophet, or of each one of the elders." "<b>Counsels from afar.</b> From ancient days, and the meaning is joined with the making." "<b>[Faith, truly].</b> And they appeared in faithfulness, and the word אמונה is like an artisan [אומן], as in 'YHWH my strength and my stronghold' (Jeremiah 15:19)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {2 "Ibn Ezra reads אמונה as cognate with אומן (artisan/craftsman), drawing the parallel to Jeremiah 15:19 where מעוזי appears; the lemma bracketed as in the source."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:04.263334186Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}